From fc2211a13c57f9528bf6e740fb0d1e533d3c72fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:08:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Draw the 3D view as one stereo area with two parallel
 cameras

The 3D view is a QOpenGLWidget that asks for a stereo surface: the edition's Qt calls
paintGL() once for each eye and shows the widget as a native window of its own, declared
full side by side, while the rest of the window stays one flat picture. Each eye has its
own camera, moved sideways by half the offset, with its frustum shifted so that the plane
through the middle of the mesh stays at the screen.

The offset is the largest for which every visible vertex stays inside the person's depth
limits (read through libstereo-declare from the top level's surface and scaled to the
width of the view), with no setting. The maths is in stereofit.cpp and is tested against
an independent projection in tests/stereofit-test.cpp. Save Image and Copy Image take one eye, the left, at the size of the view. On X11 (Xwayland) the same widget is the stereo area, with the limits read from the declared child window.


Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
